Error [jet.MoveWithoutMarker]: `consume` takes `value`, but `value` is used again later
  --> tests/ui/ownership_call_consume_provenance.jet:7:13
    |
  7 |     consume(value)
    |             ^^^^^
  --> tests/ui/ownership_call_consume_provenance.jet:8:11
    |
  8 |     print(value)
    |           ^^^^^ `value` is used again here
 Why: `consume` takes ownership of this argument, and a call never copies on its own, so `value` has no value after this call
 Fix: Write `value.copy()` to pass a copy and keep `value`, or reorder so this call is the last use of `value`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0209
